1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Agent Context Across Platform. Share the session context, and let another person
continue the work.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:25,333
When an investigation pauses, can a teammate pick up where your agent stopped and
reproduce its context and capability? Our project packages the task, history,
selected files, capability requirements, and next steps into a reviewed handoff,
so work can continue without starting over.

3
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:38,625
The challenge goes beyond copying text. Agent formats differ, files and tools may
be missing, and permissions do not transfer. We also need to protect sensitive
information and make unknowns visible.

4
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:53,542
Ideally, the sender installs once and shares in one reviewed action. The recipient
opens a controlled link and continues in their own agent. Capture, redaction,
approval, and validation stay behind that simple experience.

5
00:00:53,542 --> 00:01:12,167
The current solution uses a central server to manage session snapshots and sharing
links. We implemented this server-side workflow first. It can be hosted in a Web
App once production controls are in place. Next, we will leverage SharePoint and
OneDrive for secure, compliance-aligned file sharing.

6
00:01:12,167 --> 00:01:24,208
The flow begins with a share request for the current investigation. This first
screen shows OneDrive intent, not a completed cloud upload. The demonstration then
uses the handoff server.

7
00:01:24,208 --> 00:01:34,208
The proposed cloud path asks for specific recipients. This is an audience-
selection prompt, not evidence that cloud access has already been granted.

8
00:01:34,208 --> 00:01:46,458
The review shows the selected provider, destination, and omitted material. Secret
detection is only an aid. Publication waits for the human to approve the exact
contents and destination.

9
00:01:46,458 --> 00:01:58,833
After approval, the server returns a JSON snapshot and link. This is a reviewed
summary, not the complete live runtime. The address shown here is the test
instance of that service.

10
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:10,958
The recipient supplies the snapshot link and selects Copilot and a workspace.
Historical context can be imported, but source credentials, permissions, and tool
connections do not transfer.

11
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:23,542
The recorded output reports restored context and a dataset match. It also
discloses an access denial: popularity statistics came from cached rankings. No
SQL was run.

12
00:02:23,542 --> 00:02:39,708
Next, we will leverage SharePoint and OneDrive as a security- and compliance-
aligned file-sharing foundation. The rollout will use approved identities, scoped
recipients, and organizational data controls, with validation against tenant
security and compliance requirements.

13
00:02:39,708 --> 00:02:48,708
Contact our team to collaborate on the next phase: a simpler handoff that keeps
security, permissions, and evidence visible.
